@extends('layouts.app')
@section('path')/features/dump@endsection
@section('robots')noindex,follow@endsection

@section('title')@@dump@endsection

@section('content')
  <h1>@@dump</h1>
  <p><code>@@dump</code> prints a value while you develop, and then rendering continues. It shows the expression, then the value as a tree, laid out as Symfony's VarDumper does. Each array or object shows its size, such as <code>array:3</code>, and its entries are indented under it. Click a line to fold it. Each part has its own colour.</p>
  <p>Debug helpers render only in development builds. A release build never shows them.</p>
<pre class="line-numbers"><code class="language-blade">@@dump($post)</code></pre>
  <h3>Live example</h3>
  @dump($post)
  @dump($tags)
  <p>Rendering continued after the dumps.</p>
@endsection
